## 🎨 Icon Styles

Font Awesome provides multiple styles:

### Solid (Default)
```dart
FaIcon(FontAwesomeIcons.heart)        // Solid filled heart
FaIcon(FontAwesomeIcons.solidHeart)   // Explicit solid
```

### Regular (Outlined)
```dart
FaIcon(FontAwesomeIcons.regularHeart) // Outlined heart
```

### Brands (Social Media & Companies)
```dart
FaIcon(FontAwesomeIcons.google)
FaIcon(FontAwesomeIcons.facebook)
FaIcon(FontAwesomeIcons.twitter)
```

**Use solid for primary actions, regular for secondary elements.**

---

## 🔍 Finding Icons

1. Visit [fontawesome.com/icons](https://fontawesome.com/icons)
2. Search for concept (e.g., "education", "document", "user")
3. Copy the name and convert to camelCase
4. Use with `FontAwesomeIcons.camelCaseName`

**Example:**
- Website shows: "book-open-reader"
- Dart constant: `FontAwesomeIcons.bookOpenReader`

---

## 🚫 What NOT to Use

### ❌ Material Icons - FORBIDDEN
```dart
// NEVER use Material Icons
Icon(Icons.home)           // ❌ BAD
Icon(Icons.person)         // ❌ BAD
Icon(Icons.settings)       // ❌ BAD
```

### ⚠️ SvgIcons - LEGACY (Deprecated)
```dart
// DO NOT use in new features
SvgIcons.home(size: 24)    // ⚠️ LEGACY - existing code only
SvgIcons.courses()         // ⚠️ LEGACY - existing code only
```

**SvgIcons class exists ONLY for backward compatibility.**
- Do not use in new features
- Do not refactor existing code that uses it
- Will remain in codebase indefinitely to avoid breaking changes

